# Signing material — must never be committed.
# The release keystore and its passwords were previously published in this repo.
*.jks
android/keystore.properties
!android/keystore.properties.example

# Firebase config files ARE versioned on purpose.
#
# google-services.json and GoogleService-Info.plist are not secrets: they ship
# inside every published APK/IPA and Google documents them as app identifiers.
# What protects the project is the package name + signing SHA-1 binding, not the
# secrecy of these files. Versioning them keeps every machine (and CI) building
# with a plain `git pull`.
#
# The Firebase *service account* key is a different matter entirely: it grants
# send rights over the whole project and must never be committed. It lives only
# in the server environment (FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_BASE64).
firebase-adminsdk*.json
**/firebase-adminsdk*.json

